        "id": 129817,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-30T18:24:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>They do if you use an attack+1 token to negate an attack-1 token. &nbsp;Attack -1 tokens just have to be used on your next attack. &nbsp;Attack +1 tokens are your choice to use on an stack against a specific target</p><p>edit: I've looked at rulebook and see no mention of them automatically canceling each other out. &nbsp; While it is Luther listing that as a response, he is wrong that it is in the rulebook. &nbsp;</p>",
